          "turn_index": 0,
          "type": "turn",
          "question": "I smoke and I have been diagnosed with COPD.",
          "answer": "I'm sorry to hear about your COPD diagnosis. Quitting smoking is an important topic with COPD, but the guidance I searched doesn't directly answer how to do it.\n\nThe most relevant passage is from the document \"guideline-copd-diagnosis-and-stepwise-management.\" It explains that COPD is confirmed by a breathing test and that smoking is the most common exposure linked to it. It also says that symptoms and flare-ups (exacerbations) are assessed alongside the breathing test result. The passage I received was cut off, so it doesn't cover treatment or quitting support.\n\nA second document, \"guideline-coronary-artery-disease-secondary-prevention,\" says smoking cessation is the largest changeable risk factor after heart disease, and that combined behavioural and medicine support works better than advice alone. That guidance is about heart disease, not COPD, so I can't apply it to your situation.\n\nThe other results covered cholesterol, reflux and diabetes, so they don't apply here.\n\nYour diagnosis and quitting plan are best discussed with the clinician who diagnosed you. They can explain your test results, your options for stopping smoking, and what support is available. Ask them specifically about which quitting aids suit you.\n\nIf you tell me what you'd like to understand, such as what COPD is, how it's diagnosed, or what questions to bring to your appointment, I can search for that.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
