          "session_id": "full-mt-m-010",
          "turn_index": 2,
          "type": "turn",
          "question": "How much difference does it make to how breathless I get?",
          "answer": "The guidance I searched doesn't say how much stopping smoking changes how breathless you feel. The earlier point about lung function decline doesn't answer this, because the results don't link lung function to breathlessness directly.\n\nThe document \"lifestyle-copd-activity\" says that breathlessness often leads people to avoid activity, which weakens their muscles and makes breathlessness worse. It says that much of the improvement available in COPD comes from breaking this cycle, and it treats exercise as a therapy. It also says that how well the lungs work (measured by a breathing test) correlates only loosely with how a person actually feels.\n\nYour clinician or a pulmonary rehabilitation team can talk with you about how breathlessness is likely to change for you. They can also help you plan activity safely.\n\nSeek emergency care straight away if you have breathlessness at rest, breathlessness that starts suddenly, trouble speaking in full sentences, blue or grey lips or fingertips, or chest pain with breathlessness. This comes from the document \"red-flag-severe-breathing-difficulty.\"\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
